VERDICT: PASS on root election + detection + traffic; alternate-path step UNMEASURED (see below)

UNMEASURED, same reason as 38152: the physical ring spans three VLANs and the
two legs meet the DUT in vlan 1 and vlan 10, which do not bridge on the DUT,
so there is no layer-2 alternate path to fail over to. The ring was NOT closed
for this case -- 38152 established that closing it is unsafe while a leg can
sit inside a down aggregator, and the alternate-path assertion is unreachable
either way.
